  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed Value near $15.95B (-1.5% 30D) keeps on-chain RWA exposure in a holding pattern\u2014tokenization momentum is still news- and pipeline-driven until distributed value breaks range. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/regulation/2026-09-01-sec-seeks-update-1970s-era-transfer-agent-rules-for-blockchain-age-413278\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SEC seeks to update its 1970s-era transfer agent rules for the blockchain age</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows.</li><li><strong>Tokenized T-bill supply is still expanding through new products:</strong> That usually shows up first as new issuer and product supply, then as higher distributed value and denser collateral-style use across networks and platforms. Related: <a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxQWWxoYVFPeG9UTWlfUE4yaDNpX1RaVEE5aGZIY2NBNW92dmtLamF2ME5ObURydEVLR280RjNiRXRETV9pVjBxNWNodEYzNW0xdS1UeW0wcmNJR0RVZFlFU0NjaWpiMWJNRWs3Nm94Zk0zdFlkOW93cGJYREs2TXVjVUIzNkhOeTVjUHBKaV9YNkhtUng5NlZ3M1ZnbW0xMV9RVWs0bFE4dm5aWEJVc3I4QjlSeGNUMy1iRGR4WA?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NYSE owner ICE taps tZERO for tokenized securities push, takes stake in firm</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/thailand-sec-retail-overseas-crypto-derivatives?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Thailand SEC proposes retail access to regulated overseas crypto derivatives</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
